ator likely uses the standard ARC color palette, excluding the background color. Therefore, given a grid color of 5, the palette is [1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9]. Using 5 in the generated cell would be indistinguishable, and look like a glitch. Now I'm checking the final test grid colors.\n\n\n\n**Verifying Color Assignments**\n\nI've now analyzed the test grid's color assignments based on my established assumptions. I've verified the color sequence: Block (1,1) is color 1 (blue). Block (2,2) is color 2 (red). Block (3,3) is color 3 (green). Block (4,4) is color 4 (yellow). The final diagonal block, (5,5), is color 6 (magenta). Everything seems consistent and I'm ready to move on.\n\n\n",
